Source landscape: The 2023 documentary universe is broad and multilingual, spanning government records, international monitoring, courts, human-rights organizations, women’s-rights groups, disaster-response records, and reputable reporting. The strongest candidate families concern torture and detention, earthquake emergency powers, security-force conduct, protest policing, disappearances, vulnerable-group protection, oversight, and domestic violence. Search discovery produced more than 30 distinct candidates; records remain unopened because search-result discovery is not evidence inspection.

